---
import SiteLayout from '~/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

// NOTE FOR MAINTAINERS
// This is a general website Terms of Service for a working ranch offering
// guided horseback trail rides, riding lessons, kids camps, ranch stays,
// and equine-assisted coaching in Poway, CA. It is NOT a substitute for a
// signed liability waiver / release of liability that every rider (or a
// parent/guardian for minors) must sign in person or through FareHarbor's
// waiver tool before mounting a horse — that separate document, not this
// page, is what actually carries the weight in the event of an injury claim.
// California does not have a dedicated equine-activity-immunity statute like
// many other states; California courts generally enforce liability releases
// for ordinary negligence in recreational activities (see Tunkl v. Regents
// and its progeny) but will not enforce a release for gross negligence,
// recklessness, or intentional misconduct, and will not enforce one against
// a minor without a parent/guardian's signature. Have a California-licensed
// attorney experienced in equine/recreational liability review this page
// and your separate waiver form before relying on either. Bump LAST_UPDATED
// whenever this page or the waiver process changes.

const LAST_UPDATED = 'September 18, 2026';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Terms of Service',
  description:
    'The terms that govern use of sandiegotrailcompany.com and participation in guided trail rides, lessons, camps, ranch stays, and events at San Diego Trail Company in Poway, CA.',
  robots: { index: true, follow: true },
};

const h2 = 'font-family:\'Cormorant Garamond\',serif;font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);font-weight:400;color:#3b2314;';
const h3 = 'font-size:17px;font-weight:600;color:#3b2314;';
---

<SiteLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- Header band (dark so the transparent nav stays readable) -->
  <section class="px-6 lg:px-12 pt-32 pb-16 lg:pt-40 lg:pb-20" style="background-color:#3b2314;">
    <div class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto">
      <div class="uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-4" style="font-size:11px;color:#8a9e7b;">Legal</div>
      <h1
        class="text-white mb-5"
        style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:clamp(44px,7vw,72px);font-weight:300;line-height:1.05;"
      >
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-white" style="font-size:16px;opacity:0.75;">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 lg:px-12 py-16 lg:py-24" style="background-color:#f5f0e8;">
    <div
      class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto flex flex-col gap-10"
      style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#2c2c2c;"
    >
      <p>
        These Terms of Service (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;) govern your use of <strong>sandiegotrailcompany.com</strong> and
        your participation in any guided trail ride, riding lesson, kids camp, equine-assisted coaching session, ranch
        stay, or event (each an &ldquo;Activity&rdquo;) offered by San Diego Trail Company (&ldquo;we,&rdquo;
        &ldquo;us,&rdquo; &ldquo;our&rdquo;). By using this site or booking an Activity, you agree to these Terms. If
        you do not agree, please do not use the site or book with us.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          San Diego Trail Company operates a working ranch at 14875 Mina De Oro, Poway, CA 92064. We can be reached at
          <a href="tel:+18587486441" style="color:#c49a3c;">858-748-6441</a> or
          <a href="mailto:ride@powayequestriancenter.com" style="color:#c49a3c;" class="break-all"
            >ride@powayequestriancenter.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Inherent risks of equine activities</h2>
        <p>
          Horses are large, powerful animals with independent will, and no amount of skill, training, or care can
          eliminate the unpredictability of working with them. <strong
            >By participating in any Activity involving a horse, you acknowledge and accept that you may be exposed
            to risks including, but not limited to:</strong
          >
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 pl-5" style="list-style:disc;">
          <li>
            A horse bucking, rearing, biting, kicking, bolting, stumbling, or reacting unpredictably to sounds,
            movement, other animals, terrain, or unfamiliar objects.
          </li>
          <li>Falling or being thrown from a horse, or a horse falling, rolling, or losing its footing.</li>
          <li>
            Collision with, or being struck, stepped on, or crushed by, a horse or another rider, whether mounted or
            on foot.
          </li>
          <li>
            Uneven, steep, muddy, rocky, or otherwise hazardous natural terrain on guided canyon and backcountry
            trails.
          </li>
          <li>Exposure to sun, heat, cold, insects, wildlife, and other outdoor and ranch-environment conditions.</li>
          <li>
            A rider's own action or inaction, misjudgment, failure to follow instructions, or physical limitations.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <strong
            >These risks cannot be eliminated regardless of the care taken to avoid injuries, and you voluntarily
            assume them by choosing to participate.</strong
          > Riders should have no known cardiac, respiratory, back, or other medical condition that could be aggravated
          by horseback riding, and should tell staff about any condition, pregnancy, or physical limitation before
          mounting.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Liability waiver required before participation</h2>
        <p>
          Every participant &mdash; or, for a minor, that minor's parent or legal guardian &mdash; must read, sign,
          and submit our separate Liability Waiver and Release of Claims before mounting a horse or beginning any
          Activity, in addition to agreeing to these Terms. That waiver form, not this page alone, is the document
          releasing us from liability for the inherent risks described above and for our ordinary negligence to the
          fullest extent allowed by California law. We will provide it to you before your visit or ask you to sign it
          on arrival; a ride or lesson cannot begin until it is completed.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Nothing in these Terms or in that waiver releases us from liability for gross negligence, recklessness, or
          intentional misconduct, or limits any right that cannot be waived under California law.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Eligibility, fitness, and rider conduct</h2>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 pl-5" style="list-style:disc;">
          <li>
            Guided trail rides are generally offered to riders age 7 and up; some Activities have their own age,
            weight, height, or experience requirements, which we will tell you at booking.
          </li>
          <li>Riders under 18 must be accompanied by, or have written consent from, a parent or legal guardian.</li>
          <li>
            We may refuse or end participation for anyone who appears intoxicated, is unable to follow safety
            instructions, or whose conduct puts themselves, other guests, staff, or a horse at risk &mdash; no refund
            is owed in that case.
          </li>
          <li>
            You must follow our guides' instructions at all times, wear any safety equipment provided, and disclose
            any relevant medical condition, medication, pregnancy, or limitation before the Activity begins.
          </li>
          <li>Closed-toe shoes with a heel are required to ride. Long pants are strongly recommended.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Bookings, payment, and cancellation</h2>
        <p>
          Activities are booked and paid for through <strong>FareHarbor</strong>, our third-party reservation
          provider, under FareHarbor's own terms in addition to these Terms. Pricing, deposit, cancellation, and
          weather/reschedule policies are shown at the time of booking in FareHarbor's checkout flow &mdash; please
          read them before you pay, since they control refund eligibility. Gift certificates sold through our shop
          are redeemable toward Activities and are non-refundable for cash once purchased.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by California law, and except for our gross negligence, recklessness, or
          intentional misconduct: (a) San Diego Trail Company, its owners, employees, guides, and agents are not
          liable for any injury, death, property damage, or other loss arising from or related to an Activity or use
          of this website; and (b) if liability is found despite the foregoing, our total liability to you for any
          claim arising out of an Activity or this website will not exceed the amount you paid us for that Activity.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We are not liable for indirect, incidental, consequential, or punitive damages, including lost enjoyment of
          a trip or event, even if we have been advised such damages are possible. Some jurisdictions do not allow
          certain limitations on liability, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify and hold us harmless from any claim, damage, or expense (including reasonable
          attorney's fees) arising from your breach of these Terms, your violation of any law, or your negligent or
          intentional act or omission during an Activity or while on our property.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Photography and video</h2>
        <p>
          We may photograph or video guests during Activities for our marketing, website, and social media, and by
          participating you consent to that use without compensation, unless you tell staff in writing beforehand
          that you decline. To request removal of an existing photo or video, contact us using the details below.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Using this website</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to use sandiegotrailcompany.com only for lawful purposes: not to interfere with its operation or
          security, not to scrape or misuse its content, and not to submit false or fraudulent booking or contact
          information. Content on this site &mdash; text, photos, and design &mdash; belongs to San Diego Trail
          Company or its licensors and may not be reused without permission. See our
          <a href="/contact/privacy-policy/" style="color:#c49a3c;">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle information
          collected through the site.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
        <p>
          This website and our Activities are provided &ldquo;as is.&rdquo; We do not warrant that the site will be
          uninterrupted or error-free, and we make no warranty about the outcome or fitness of any Activity for a
          particular purpose beyond what is stated at booking.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules.
          Any dispute arising out of these Terms or an Activity will be resolved in the state or federal courts
          located in San Diego County, California, and you consent to that venue and jurisdiction.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Severability</h2>
        <p>
          If any part of these Terms is found unenforceable, the rest remains in full effect, and the unenforceable
          part will be read to most closely reflect its original intent within the limits of the law.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms as our Activities, policies, or the law change. We will revise the date at the
          top of this page when we do. Continuing to use the site or book an Activity after an update means you
          accept the revised Terms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Contact us</h2>
        <p>Questions about these Terms:</p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          San Diego Trail Company<br />
          14875 Mina De Oro, Poway, CA 92064<br />
          <a href="tel:+18587486441" style="color:#c49a3c;">858-748-6441</a><br />
          <a href="mailto:ride@powayequestriancenter.com" style="color:#c49a3c;" class="break-all"
            >ride@powayequestriancenter.com</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
